# The vendored original and its inputs are byte-exact artefacts: runs.json records
# the SHA-256 of each one, and the checks in README.md compare against those digests.
# They are DOS files (CRLF) in DOS codepages — the source is CP1251, the .dat files
# CP866 — so any end-of-line normalisation on checkout would break both the digests
# and the fixed-form column layout the compiler depends on. -text switches off EOL
# conversion in both directions; diffs stay available, mojibake and all.
PropStructv3.for -text
inputs/*.dat     -text

# Probes are the same kind of artefact: a DOS input and the DOS report the original
# wrote for it. The test asserts against literal lines of the .m, so a normalised
# checkout would break the assertion rather than merely look wrong.
probes/*.dat     -text
probes/*.m       -text
